course: dictionary
lesson: 8226
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. «You stay well away from a big machine that is reversing, because the driver cannot see you.» Here reversing means moving backwards, because the driver cannot see behind.
explain: Reverse can also mean to turn something the other way round or to change it to the opposite. «Reverse the order» means put the items in the opposite order. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: As a noun, reverse means the opposite or the back side. «It's the reverse of what I expected» means it is the opposite of your guess. «Look at the reverse of the coin» means look at its back side.
fact: Reverse means to go backwards, especially in a car.
fact: To reverse something means to turn it the other way round or change it to the opposite.
fact: «The reverse» means the opposite, as in «quite the reverse».
fact: «Reversing lights» show that a car is going backwards.
fact: Some changes can be reversed, like melting ice, but burning cannot be reversed.
exercise: «You stay well away from a big machine that is reversing, because the driver cannot see you.» What does reversing mean here? | *Going backwards | Turning round to face the sun | Driving very fast | Stopping for a long rest
exercise: In maths, adding reverses subtracting. What does reverses mean here? | *Undoes, does the opposite of | Makes the same as | Sorts into order | Doubles
exercise: Someone says the answer is «quite the reverse» of what you expected. What does that mean? | Almost the same | Very noisy | *Completely the opposite | Slightly different and slower
test: «Please reverse the order of the words.» What does reverse the order mean? | Read them out loud | Count the words | Write them in bold | *Put them the other way round
test: «Look at the reverse of the coin.» What does reverse mean in this sentence? | The side that shines | *The back side | A small metal ring | The front side with the head
exam: Jayden says reverse always means going backwards. Is he right? | Yes, reverse only ever means going backwards | No, reverse means happy | Yes, and a reverse image search is only for cars | *No, it can also mean the opposite or the back of a coin, so context helps
